  <section id="compare">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <h2>Penny against what's available in Israel.</h2>
        <p>We checked what each product says about itself on its website or in the app store. Where we found nothing we wrote "Not stated", which doesn't mean the feature is missing. Where others do better than us, we said so. "Bank app" was checked at Hapoalim, Leumi and Pepper.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="compare" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Comparison table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr">Capability</span></th><th scope="col">Penny</th><th scope="col">RiseUp</th><th scope="col">Shavve</th><th scope="col">Moneytor</th><th scope="col">FamilyBiz</th><th scope="col">Cover</th><th scope="col">MyFinanda</th><th scope="col">Bank app</th><th scope="col">Excel</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Price per month</th><td>₪0</td><td>₪55, after a free month</td><td>₪19 (Pro), after 30 free days</td><td>₪49 (Premium). Manual basic: ₪0</td><td>Not published. Basic: ₪0</td><td>₪0</td><td>No monthly plan. ₪49.90 for 3 months</td><td>Part of the account</td><td>₪0 or part of Office</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Price per year</th><td>₪0</td><td>No yearly plan published. 12 months: ₪660</td><td>₪199 (Pro)</td><td>₪490 (Premium)</td><td>₪349.90 (Premium)</td><td>₪0</td><td>No yearly plan published. 2 × ₪89.90 per half year: ₪179.80</td><td>Part of the account</td><td>₪0 or part of Office</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">All banks and cards in one place</th><td><b class="y">Yes</b> 18 institutions, in beta</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> in Premium</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td>Not mentioned</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> 15 institutions</td><td><b class="n">No</b> only that bank</td><td>Manual</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">How it connects to the bank</th><td>Your bank password, encrypted on your computer. Or a file</td><td>Licensed open banking, no password</td><td>Licensed open banking, no password</td><td>Licensed open banking, no password</td><td>Licensed open banking, no password</td><td>Pension clearing house and Ministry of Finance</td><td>Licensed open banking, read only</td><td>Built in</td><td>Typing or copying</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Where your data lives</th><td>On your computer</td><td>With the company</td><td>With the company</td><td>With the company</td><td>With the company</td><td>With the company</td><td>With the company</td><td>With the bank</td><td>In your file</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Licensed as a financial information service</th><td><b class="n">No</b> software you run, not a service</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td>Not stated</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td>Supervised by the Bank of Israel</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Budget and cash flow</th><td><b class="y">Yes</b> budgets, envelopes, balance forecast</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> monthly cash flow</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> budgets</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> monthly cash flow</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> spending and income targets</td><td>Not stated</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> budget targets</td><td>In some banks</td><td>Manual</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pension and insurance</th><td><b class="y">Yes</b> pension and investments from 8 providers, insurance list</td><td>Not stated</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> in paid packages</td><td>Pension yes, insurance not stated</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td>Savings and investments. Pension not stated</td><td>At that bank only</td><td>Manual</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Where you could save</th><td><b class="y">Yes</b> fees, double insurance, bank fees, tax refund</td><td>Not stated</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> fee comparison and paid services</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> pension fees</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> product comparison and cheaper insurance</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> pension and insurance recommendations</td><td>Not stated</td><td>Not stated</td><td><b class="n">No</b></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Partner and family</th><td><b class="y">Yes</b> a profile each</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> partner free</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> shared household</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> family subscription</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td>Not stated</td><td>Not stated</td><td>Joint account</td><td>Shared file</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A person to talk to</th><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> cash-flow experts, on WhatsApp</td><td>Referral to paid experts</td><td>Not stated</td><td>Insurance and pension through a licensed agency</td><td>An AI agent, also on WhatsApp</td><td>Not stated</td><td>A banker</td><td><b class="n">No</b></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">AI</th><td><b class="y">Yes</b> your choice, local too</td><td>Not stated</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> connect your own AI</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> API and MCP in Premium</td><td>Not stated</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> AI agent</td><td>Not stated</td><td>"Smart analysis" at Hapoalim</td><td><b class="n">No</b></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Phone app</th><td><b class="n">No</b> web on your home network, plus shortcuts</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> iOS, Android and web</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> iOS, Android</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> iOS and web</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> iOS, Android</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> app and WhatsApp</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b> iOS</td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Works with the computer off</th><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Open source</th><td><b class="y">Yes</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td><td><b class="n">No</b></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <p class="note">Checked on 22 November 2026. Prices and features change, so check the sites themselves. Sources: <a href="https://www.riseup.co.il/subscription/">RiseUp</a>, <a href="https://www.riseup.co.il/questions/">RiseUp FAQ</a>, <a href="https://www.shavve.io/he">Shavve</a>, <a href="https://moneytor.ai/">Moneytor</a>, <a href="https://www.familybiz.co.il/">FamilyBiz</a>, <a href="https://www.cover.co.il/">Cover</a>, <a href="https://apps.apple.com/il/app/id785487890">MyFinanda</a>, <a href="https://apps.apple.com/il/app/id362123205">Hapoalim</a>, <a href="https://www.leumi.co.il/leumi-digital/new-app">Leumi</a>, <a href="https://apps.apple.com/app/id1138799805">Pepper</a>. Found a mistake? <a href="https://github.com/Sergey-Bar/Penny/issues">Tell us</a> and we'll fix it.</p>
      <div class="choose"><div><h3>When to choose Penny</h3><p>You want the whole picture, including pension, insurance, tax and a forecast, with no subscription and without your data sitting with a company. You have a computer at home and don't mind a few minutes of setup.</p></div><div><h3>When to choose something else</h3><p>You want your bank connected through licensed open banking, without handing over a password, and a store app that works when your computer is off. RiseUp, Shavve, Moneytor, FamilyBiz and MyFinanda do that. For a person to guide you, look at RiseUp; to just see pension and insurance for free, look at Cover.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="limits" class="tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <h2>What isn't good enough yet.</h2>
        <p>So you can decide on the facts.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="limits">
        <li><h3>Bank sync is in beta</h3><p>It signs in to the bank's website with your password, and can break when a bank changes its site until it's fixed. File import always works. Automatic retrieval from a bank's website may break its terms of use.</p></li>
        <li><h3>No app in the store</h3><p>On your phone you open Penny over your home network and can add it to the home screen. There is no access from outside the home, on purpose.</p></li>
        <li><h3>The computer has to be on</h3><p>Sync runs while the computer is on. You set up the backup, to a folder your own cloud syncs.</p></li>
        <li><h3>The installers aren't signed</h3><p>Windows and Mac show a warning on first install. Updates themselves are signed and checked before they install.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
